						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=330">Garlin</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">4/10/2001 - 9:59 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=251">Garlin Treehorn</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=550">Joobay Mujuro</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Id like to start out on a good note, We had a great turn out for monday's Unrest Raid.  But one thing that pissed me off was the lack of ears that i think most of the guild showed on Monday.<br />
<br />
What i think NEEDS to be done is STOP the invites for a little while, so we can get names of all who are currently in PotD and make raid groups so eveyone knows where to be and who to be with.  Second, it needs to be clearly know throughout the guild who the Officers are who are at the raid.  I on MANY occations shouted with no answers trying to clean up the mess.  When an officer tells you to do somthing you should do it.  Every Raid should have a Raid leader how spouts out the orders, i have no problem leading raids its just that when no one listens or cares i get a little pissed off like most of us did.  We need to have designated pullers, a few people volenteer to be pullers and it is well know who is the puller for that raid.  We kicked everythings ass in Unrest but i would have liked to seen it with a little more style and not a big mess of corpses Mobs and our own<br />
<br />
 I would like to close this by saying Not all raids are for PLing/exp its for the items we get and give to our other members.  Exp in a raid is great but if you want exp dont attend the raid thats how i see it.<br />
<br />
P.S. if this is hard to read give me a break its 1 am in the morrning						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=247">IronWolf</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">4/10/2001 - 11:15 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=211">Lastrae Soulsend</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=250">Nordrin</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														With no organization Raids are pointless. <br />
<br />
All raids should have as follows:<br />
<br />
Group1<br />
Warrior - Best Tank<br />
Warrior - Assist Main Tank<br />
Cleric - Your responsible for healing Tank 1<br />
Cleric - Your Responsible for healing Tank 2<br />
Chanter - Crowd Control..You know your job :)<br />
Bard/Druid/Wizzy/Mage/Necro - Bard Battle enchanced songs..<br />
Druid - Back heal / SNARE DUTY<br />
Wizzy - Unleash your nukes but ONLY when foe is at half..if you unleash to early you will be aggro<br />
Necro DOT / Feeder (mana to clerics) Pet assists main tank<br />
<br />
Group2<br />
<br />
This will be composed of your casters..One cleric to watch over..<br />
<br />
Basicly Your most important guildies are the TANKS..You can be the best druid or the best Necro but you mean nothing in raids :) SOrry if this is hurting feelings but get use to it. EQ is party based :)<br />
<br />
Listening to your Team leads and Raid Leader is a MUST. One slip can mean the total loss of camp. Even worse trying to get your body after the Sh*t hits the fan is a pain. No one expects for you to get it perfect cause lord knows there 50s levels that STILL don't get it :)<br />
<br />
Well enjoy..<br />
<br />
My 2 cents..<br />
Soulsend<br />
(Will be here if needed...)						</td>
					</tr>
