				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=1299">Techie</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">4/11/2001 - 11:57 AM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
										
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														I suggest that we plan the groups on here in advance of the raid so when people show up they know exactly where they are going and what they are doing.  Maybe have it set up so that people who want to group together can and then fill the ranks after that.  Next if we raid an area that is so nicely seperated we should use it to our advantage.  Higher lvls take out the more dangerous areas and stay there allowing the lower lvls to get stuff that they can kill.  Also I noticed on this last raid that some of our groups had people from other guilds, while I don't think this is a problem we should make sure that all guild members are grouped first.  Thanks for listening to me rant.						</td>
